A||||4||JohnF||Front Compartment Light||||5||
Z||000000||JohnF||10-23-2001||04:42 PM||||Seems as if a lot of Fieros have a front compartment light located near the blower.  Any clues as to just exactly where this light is or hints as to how to find the socket?  Said to use the same bulb as the side marker lights.||||reg||5
Z||000001||Dan010||10-23-2001||04:58 PM||||Found mine a couple of weeks ago, kind of hid<BR>under area for windshield wiper,with light buld pointing down, passanger side<BR>next to two square parts and a/c charge connections. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||88CoupeV6||10-23-2001||05:19 PM||||In the wire harness to the blower. It will be next to the relays on the firewall. Some late 88's don't have the light harness as Pontiac ran out. Also the light will only go on when the parking lights are on.<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig.jpg">    <BR>:D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000003||JohnF||10-23-2001||05:47 PM||||Unbelieveable but true!  I found it!  <P>I just checked the '88 Coupe I bought new in Nov. 1987.  The receptacle is there but no light bulb.  I checked my '85GT and it lights like it was new!  Light comes on anytime parking light switch and/or headlight switch is turned on.<P>This forum rocks!  Thanks!||||reg||10
Z||000004||danny boy||10-23-2001||11:11 PM||||(running out to check mine).....&lt;check&gt;.....<BR>Hey! I do have one!!!! ||||reg||1
